  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_c7a5372fb84445faa5de0693308f3362",
      "statement": "NodeBindings integrates libuv with Chromium's message loop using a dedicated embed thread: it waits on a semaphore, blocks in a platform-specific PollEvents() (epoll on Linux, select on macOS, IOCP on Windows), then posts UvRunOnce to the main thread's task runner, which runs uv_run(UV_RUN_NOWAIT) and re-arms the embed thread.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://shell/common/node_bindings.cc#L860-L995",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3b26174a0042f97314808b09f24a1eb9b9af16c3ba378e39576ef0176fb0572e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://shell/common/node_bindings_linux.cc#L22-L32",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ddb60ac867fbee70a5529a16d4ae4136817d7bb2e986749c656aeb578f532d9a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://shell/common/node_bindings_mac.cc#L24-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ca5ac59ac81d68e71a80f76bc089bcc451f08a92285c84b8303debb8fd2488ba:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://shell/common/node_bindings_win.cc#L32-L50",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2b4748b686836834b51f2c425cc13a9c34bd85d2291253c9faf92732465a70e5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1e155b4ac74745629ee1d564c1547d86",
      "statement": "Browser, renderer and utility processes share uv_default_loop(), while each Web Worker gets its own uv_loop_t; every loop is configured with UV_LOOP_INTERRUPT_ON_IO_CHANGE.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://shell/common/node_bindings.cc#L514-L529",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9a809a993a2d67742b3f708273c27f196883884cacbbe9d79ffa5eb11ed9a59d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d7d784f29c3c42a7beb7dcf9b8bd3ed8",
      "statement": "NodeBindings::Initialize calls node::InitializeOncePerProcess with flags that stop Node from initializing V8, cppgc and its own V8 platform, and disables the WASM trap handler because Chromium already enabled it; NODE_OPTIONS is only honored when the node_options fuse is enabled.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://shell/common/node_bindings.cc#L587-L651",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:536ef0f3cb0482831be710e1b8f4ab5158f2ee1a7a82a27379518afd0e28c8a8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8d52c6be14254da8b2092bbafafe4938",
      "statement": "In renderer and worker environments Node is created with kNoBrowserGlobals, kNoCreateInspector and kNoRegisterESMLoader because Blink provides those, and renderers keep Blink's promise-rejection, message-listener and prepareStackTrace callbacks instead of Node's; the node_cli_inspect fuse disables the SIGUSR1 debug handler.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://shell/common/node_bindings.cc#L715-L790",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:033ccb1c5a91f21872d67b4f28fe3738a0e20fd9dc582b1b50665686893d0168:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_dfda896aff3a4ea9b87181d688de2cc0",
      "statement": "The browser and utility processes use the explicit microtasks policy, and in the browser a MicrotasksRunner task observer lets Node perform the microtask checkpoint after each Chromium UI task; in renderers the isolate's policy is left as Blink's and is switched to explicit only while UvRunOnce runs.",
